I need help ASAP!

267
00:20:44,840 --> 00:20:45,720
Where should I go?

268
00:20:45,800 --> 00:20:47,520
THE CROW CLUB

269
00:21:03,160 --> 00:21:04,040
Nugget!

270
00:21:06,320 --> 00:21:07,640
Like this. Spread your wings like this.

271
00:21:08,640 --> 00:21:10,760
Come on. Nugget! Nugget! Nugget!

272
00:21:16,360 --> 00:21:18,760
You think Linda won't see it?

273
00:21:20,440 --> 00:21:22,280
What did you take pity on
and bring home this time?

274
00:21:22,360 --> 00:21:24,400
Hey! Where are you going?

275
00:21:24,480 --> 00:21:26,280
You and that chick
will both get kicked out.

276
00:21:26,360 --> 00:21:28,920
Hey, are you really

277
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:31,960
going to leave it outside
in the wind and rain?

278
00:21:32,040 --> 00:21:33,960
You heartless jerk.

279
00:21:35,720 --> 00:21:37,520
You named the chick "Nugget."

280
00:21:37,600 --> 00:21:38,960
I'm sure it'll grow up just fine.

281
00:21:40,320 --> 00:21:41,800
Mimi!

282
00:21:42,400 --> 00:21:43,320
Mimi!

283
00:21:43,840 --> 00:21:45,200
Mimi, where are you?

284
00:21:45,760 --> 00:21:47,520
Mi… Hey, where are you going?

285
00:21:47,600 --> 00:21:50,160
A supplier's waiting out back.
Go get the delivery.

286
00:21:50,760 --> 00:21:52,280
I'm going right now.

287
00:21:52,360 --> 00:21:53,960
- Then go!
- But…

288
00:21:54,480 --> 00:21:55,720
Hurry. You're keeping them waiting.

289
00:21:55,800 --> 00:21:58,280
- What's wrong with you?
- My back… My back hurts.

290
00:21:58,360 --> 00:21:59,480
Go!

291
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:02,360
I'm going. I'm going now.

292
00:22:02,440 --> 00:22:03,720
You go ahead, Linda.

293
00:22:03,800 --> 00:22:06,560
I'll see you off…
until you're out of sight.

294
00:22:06,640 --> 00:22:08,920
Come on! You're keeping
them waiting. Hurry!

295
00:22:09,560 --> 00:22:10,800
What's with her?

296
00:22:18,400 --> 00:22:20,720
Tangmo! Can you get the delivery for me?

297
00:22:20,800 --> 00:22:23,800
Please. I have to hide Nugget.

298
00:22:23,880 --> 00:22:26,520
Please, just for a sec. Thank you.

299
00:22:29,600 --> 00:22:31,840
Vann, you go.

300
00:22:31,920 --> 00:22:34,360
No, I'm researching universities.

301
00:22:35,040 --> 00:22:36,320
You go ahead.

302
00:22:37,760 --> 00:22:39,120
Fine. I'll go.

303
00:22:59,960 --> 00:23:00,960
Yoyeh?

304
00:23:02,400 --> 00:23:03,760
Oh, Tangmo.

305
00:23:04,720 --> 00:23:06,320
Long time no see.

306
00:23:06,400 --> 00:23:07,400
How have you been?

307
00:23:08,160 --> 00:23:09,760
What are you doing here?

308
00:23:11,520 --> 00:23:14,080
I'm delivering beer to The Crow Club.

309
00:23:14,800 --> 00:23:16,960
Today's my first day on the job.

310
00:23:18,320 --> 00:23:19,720
I'm glad to see you.

311
00:23:19,800 --> 00:23:21,840
Once you're done, you can leave.

312
00:23:21,920 --> 00:23:23,640
And don't come here again.

313
00:23:25,360 --> 00:23:27,000
Wait, Tangmo.

314
00:23:31,360 --> 00:23:33,400
Uh… It's just that…

315
00:23:33,480 --> 00:23:34,960
Sis hasn't paid for the order yet.

316
00:23:36,480 --> 00:23:37,480
Here's the bill.

317
00:23:38,840 --> 00:23:40,760
You haven't changed one damn bit.

318
00:23:40,840 --> 00:23:42,680
I'll tell Sis to transfer the money.

319
00:23:43,280 --> 00:23:46,600
As for you, leave and don't come back.

320
00:23:55,960 --> 00:23:57,800
Oh, I'm sweating.

321
00:23:58,400 --> 00:24:00,440
- Can you throw this away for me, Talay?
- Sis…

322
00:24:01,480 --> 00:24:04,240
I'm begging you.
Don't use this beer supplier again.

323
00:24:04,320 --> 00:24:05,160
I don't like them.

324
00:24:05,240 --> 00:24:07,440
He's just delivering beer.
Why don't you like him?

325
00:24:08,200 --> 00:24:10,520
I don't like the delivery guy's face.

326
00:24:10,600 --> 00:24:11,960
- I can't stand him.
- Hey!

327
00:24:13,400 --> 00:24:15,320
He's just making a delivery.

328
00:24:15,400 --> 00:24:16,680
Why do you hate him so much?

329
00:24:21,360 --> 00:24:22,480
Hey, Sis.

330
00:24:23,120 --> 00:24:24,840
You asked, and he wouldn't answer.

331
00:24:25,360 --> 00:24:27,240
I bet those two have a past.

332
00:24:28,480 --> 00:24:29,600
A past?

333
00:24:31,480 --> 00:24:32,520
A past.

334
00:24:33,040 --> 00:24:34,400
What a shame.

335
00:24:34,480 --> 00:24:39,360
If I'd gone down there earlier,
I would've seen Tangmo's past.

336
00:24:39,880 --> 00:24:41,000
Mimi!

337
00:24:41,080 --> 00:24:43,120
- Hey! Don't touch me!
- Calm down.

338
00:24:43,200 --> 00:24:45,880
- Enough.
- Talay, look! He's picking on me!

339
00:24:45,960 --> 00:24:48,160
Enough! I have a headache.

340
00:24:48,240 --> 00:24:49,760
Stop messing around.

341
00:24:50,360 --> 00:24:52,200
God, all this noise.

342
00:24:52,280 --> 00:24:54,160
You do nothing all day.

343
00:24:54,760 --> 00:24:55,840
This one's a total nutcase.

344
00:24:56,720 --> 00:25:00,040
And this one… is hotheaded
and always gets violent.

345
00:25:02,280 --> 00:25:04,360
And don't you smile.

346
00:25:04,440 --> 00:25:05,920
You're no different.

347
00:25:06,000 --> 00:25:08,040
You're supposed to be the leader,

348
00:25:08,600 --> 00:25:10,320
but you're so unpredictable.

349
00:25:10,920 --> 00:25:11,760
And this girl…

350
00:25:14,360 --> 00:25:15,680
You're fine.

351
00:25:15,760 --> 00:25:16,960
As for Phatee…

352
00:25:18,880 --> 00:25:19,720
You…

353
00:25:20,920 --> 00:25:21,920
Look at that guy.

354
00:25:23,560 --> 00:25:25,680
Won't talk, won't listen,
won't do anything.

355
00:25:25,760 --> 00:25:29,160
I'm taking all of you
to a psychiatrist once and for all.

356
00:25:30,840 --> 00:25:33,320
Sis, why do you only yell at us?

357
00:25:33,400 --> 00:25:34,640
You never yell at Vann.

358
00:25:34,720 --> 00:25:36,200
Exactly, Bro.

359
00:25:36,280 --> 00:25:38,320
And you keep calling to check on Vann.

360
00:25:38,400 --> 00:25:40,520
He's graduated from college, Sis.

361
00:25:40,600 --> 00:25:41,440
He's not a kid anymore.

362
00:25:41,520 --> 00:25:42,520
Why?

363
00:25:43,280 --> 00:25:46,760
Just because I don't yell at Vann
doesn't mean I'm not worried about him.

364
00:25:46,840 --> 00:25:49,920
I'm just less worried
about him than you guys.

365
00:25:50,480 --> 00:25:52,200
At least he has a goal.

366
00:25:52,280 --> 00:25:54,280
What goals do you guys have in life?

367
00:25:54,360 --> 00:25:56,720
Tell me. Do you have a goal in life?

368
00:25:56,800 --> 00:25:58,960
I want to be Talay's wife.

369
00:25:59,040 --> 00:26:00,760
Take it easy. Easy.

370
00:26:01,840 --> 00:26:02,880
Mimi.

371
00:26:04,240 --> 00:26:06,360
See? I have a goal now.

372
00:26:07,640 --> 00:26:09,080
Goals are meant to be pursued.

373
00:26:09,160 --> 00:26:10,080
Stop!

374
00:26:20,120 --> 00:26:21,200
- Hey.
- Hmm?

375
00:26:21,920 --> 00:26:23,840
I thought our bar was weird enough,

376
00:26:24,440 --> 00:26:26,120
but the customers are even weirder.

377
00:26:26,640 --> 00:26:27,760
Sis, look over there.

378
00:26:28,880 --> 00:26:33,320
What kind of weirdo brings a typewriter
to type at a bar every single day?

379
00:26:33,840 --> 00:26:36,760
But… I've never seen him type anything.

380
00:26:38,240 --> 00:26:39,320
Just typing away at nothing?

381
00:26:39,400 --> 00:26:40,320
Yeah.

382
00:26:41,680 --> 00:26:45,280
At first, I thought he might like Sis.

383
00:26:45,360 --> 00:26:48,120
Or if not, he must like you.

384
00:26:49,160 --> 00:26:50,880
But then I realized that wasn't it.

385
00:26:50,960 --> 00:26:52,800
I think he likes me more.

386
00:26:53,400 --> 00:26:54,360
Mimi.

387
00:26:54,960 --> 00:26:57,280
I'm begging you. Tone it down a little.

388
00:26:57,360 --> 00:26:58,760
You don't have to get jealous.

389
00:27:29,880 --> 00:27:33,440
<i>Sun, when the hell are you sending</i>
<i>the manuscript?</i>

390
00:27:33,520 --> 00:27:36,000
<i>I've put my neck on the line for you</i>
<i>to push back the deadline.</i>

391
00:27:36,080 --> 00:27:37,040
<i>I can't do it anymore.</i>

392
00:27:37,560 --> 00:27:39,200
Come on, I'm almost done writing it.

393
00:27:39,280 --> 00:27:40,440
I'll definitely send it to you.

394
00:27:41,080 --> 00:27:41,920
<i>When you say that,</i>

395
00:27:42,000 --> 00:27:44,120
<i>I'm sure you haven't</i>
<i>written a single word.</i>

396
00:27:44,200 --> 00:27:47,360
<i>Are you really going to</i>
<i>let yourself fall off this far?</i>

397
00:27:47,440 --> 00:27:50,880
<i>You used to be a romance novelist</i>
<i>with sky-high sales.</i>

398
00:27:50,960 --> 00:27:52,400
Don't say "used to" to me.

399
00:27:52,480 --> 00:27:53,680
I still am.

400
00:27:54,200 --> 00:27:55,680
<i>But if you're still stuck,</i>

401
00:27:55,760 --> 00:27:57,320
<i>"used to" is exactly what you'll be.</i>

402
00:27:57,400 --> 00:28:00,560
<i>Look. Hurry up and find some material</i>
<i>to write about.</i>

403
00:28:00,640 --> 00:28:02,560
<i>The publisher can't give you</i>
<i>much more time.</i>

404
00:28:03,320 --> 00:28:04,960
<i>Otherwise,</i>
<i>they'll terminate your contract.</i>

405
00:28:25,080 --> 00:28:26,360
The usual?

406
00:28:30,560 --> 00:28:32,280
Any other requests?

407
00:28:35,360 --> 00:28:36,560
I'd like to request you.

408
00:28:46,920 --> 00:28:50,520
They say The Crow Club takes secret jobs
and can solve any problem,

409
00:28:50,600 --> 00:28:52,920
as long as the client has money.

410
00:28:53,440 --> 00:28:55,360
Is that true or just bragging?

411
00:28:57,760 --> 00:28:59,560
Did you secretly research the club?

412
00:29:00,480 --> 00:29:03,760
You must've seen it
in the runaways' community chat.

413
00:29:04,720 --> 00:29:06,880
I just happened to hear about it.

414
00:29:06,960 --> 00:29:09,400
So, can you really solve anything?

415
00:29:11,560 --> 00:29:12,800
Pretty much anything.

416
00:29:14,160 --> 00:29:16,160
But anything beyond human ability,

417
00:29:16,720 --> 00:29:19,320
like making things disappear
or bringing people back to life,

418
00:29:20,160 --> 00:29:22,160
or playing wizard,
we don't take jobs like that.

419
00:29:22,960 --> 00:29:24,800
We don't write novels for hire either.

420
00:29:25,320 --> 00:29:27,160
That would be deceiving consumers.

421
00:29:46,840 --> 00:29:49,320
Smoking will make you die sooner.

422
00:30:07,840 --> 00:30:10,320
Candy can kill you sooner too
if you eat too much.

423
00:30:12,200 --> 00:30:14,720
True, but at least it's sweet.

424
00:30:19,640 --> 00:30:22,520
Then, what about hiring someone
to get them to fall in love,

425
00:30:22,600 --> 00:30:24,200
or hiring someone to be your lover?

426
00:30:24,720 --> 00:30:27,720
Are those within the scope
of jobs this club takes?

427
00:30:32,120 --> 00:30:34,560
You're the perfect material.

428
00:30:35,240 --> 00:30:39,440
You check all the boxes
for the character in my novel.

429
00:30:43,080 --> 00:30:44,360
I want to hire you.

430
00:30:48,400 --> 00:30:53,840
Mr. Writer, in this bar,
I'm the last person you should hire.

431
00:30:54,840 --> 00:30:56,440
Because I don't believe in "love"

432
00:30:56,520 --> 00:30:59,480
or the silly "destiny"
in your romance novels.

433
00:31:00,160 --> 00:31:01,240
Understand?

434
00:31:51,880 --> 00:31:54,600
- Can I take a photo with you?
- Sorry, but no.

435
00:32:08,480 --> 00:32:09,640
Mr. Singer,

436
00:32:10,760 --> 00:32:12,480
I really like the song you sang.

437
00:32:12,560 --> 00:32:13,880
Did you write it yourself?

438
00:32:17,240 --> 00:32:19,600
I'm forming a band to make our debut.

439
00:32:20,280 --> 00:32:22,320
And I'd like you to join the band.

440
00:32:26,480 --> 00:32:27,360
Sorry.

441
00:32:28,560 --> 00:32:29,480
Wait.

442
00:32:30,200 --> 00:32:31,160
Uh…

443
00:32:31,760 --> 00:32:32,640
How about this?

444
00:32:36,200 --> 00:32:38,080
We can start by being friends.

445
00:32:40,280 --> 00:32:41,560
I'm Ranne.

446
00:32:42,240 --> 00:32:44,240
<i>I'm Ranne.</i>

447
00:32:50,840 --> 00:32:54,280
You've seen us
in the label's trainee clips, right?

448
00:32:57,640 --> 00:32:58,720
Never.

449
00:32:59,400 --> 00:33:00,480
Sorry.

450
00:33:22,600 --> 00:33:23,840
Hello, Kao.

451
00:33:24,360 --> 00:33:25,680
We found him,

452
00:33:25,760 --> 00:33:27,920
the fifth member
to redo the audition with us.

453
00:33:28,760 --> 00:33:30,600
You'll meet him soon.

454
00:33:31,360 --> 00:33:34,040
I believe this time,

455
00:33:34,120 --> 00:33:35,840
my band will actually make our debut.

456
00:33:52,160 --> 00:33:53,120
Ranne.

457
00:34:09,320 --> 00:34:10,360
Hey, you!

458
00:34:18,639 --> 00:34:19,560
Hey!

459
00:34:21,480 --> 00:34:23,080
You pervert! What the hell are you doing?

460
00:34:27,560 --> 00:34:29,080
Vann, what are you doing?

461
00:34:29,800 --> 00:34:30,920
Lonely, little Bro?

462
00:34:31,639 --> 00:34:33,360
Can you guys stop hanging out in my room?

463
00:34:33,880 --> 00:34:35,719
My room isn't a living room.

464
00:34:36,239 --> 00:34:37,719
Your room's the most fun.

465
00:34:37,800 --> 00:34:38,920
It's the youngest one's room.

466
00:34:39,000 --> 00:34:40,560
The youngest, huh?

467
00:34:42,960 --> 00:34:47,159
Come on, we're just
looking for a place to hang out.

468
00:34:47,920 --> 00:34:50,400
You're just looking for somewhere
to eat and make me clean up.

469
00:34:51,719 --> 00:34:54,199
Hey! What are you doing?

470
00:34:54,280 --> 00:34:56,120
Tangmo, enough. Stop messing with him.

471
00:34:56,800 --> 00:34:59,240
So? How was your job today?

472
00:34:59,320 --> 00:35:01,600
Sis said you charged several times more.

473
00:35:02,120 --> 00:35:03,520
Got enough money for Japan yet?

474
00:35:05,440 --> 00:35:07,040
How much could I possibly charge?

475
00:35:07,120 --> 00:35:09,160
I only got a little extra
for getting punched.

476
00:35:10,560 --> 00:35:12,440
I was so fucking unlucky today.

477
00:35:13,080 --> 00:35:14,080
Just hang in there.

478
00:35:14,600 --> 00:35:17,120
The money for your
Engineering Master's in Japan

479
00:35:17,200 --> 00:35:18,680
is in the millions, right?

480
00:35:19,280 --> 00:35:21,600
If some well-connected kid
hadn't taken the scholarship last time,

481
00:35:22,200 --> 00:35:24,280
I wouldn't be with a bunch
of weirdos like you guys.

482
00:35:24,360 --> 00:35:25,880
Huh? Weirdos?

483
00:35:25,960 --> 00:35:28,320
- Tangmo, get him!
- Weirdos? Eat this popcorn!

484
00:35:29,920 --> 00:35:30,960
I'm not stopping him either.

485
00:35:31,040 --> 00:35:32,480
It's all over the place.

486
00:35:41,920 --> 00:35:44,680
<i>A client will come discuss</i>
<i>a job with you tomorrow.</i>

487
00:35:44,760 --> 00:35:46,720
<i>So meet at the club at ten sharp.</i>

488
00:35:48,080 --> 00:35:50,640
Jobs mean money. Money means jobs.

489
00:35:50,720 --> 00:35:52,240
Our club is pretty damn popular.

490
00:36:05,440 --> 00:36:06,640
I've got a job too.

491
00:36:07,280 --> 00:36:08,400
Me too.

492
00:36:09,920 --> 00:36:12,320
- Did you get one too?
- Yeah.

493
00:36:12,400 --> 00:36:13,360
Yeah.

494
00:36:14,040 --> 00:36:14,920
What?

495
00:36:15,440 --> 00:36:17,400
Is that the only word you know?

496
00:36:45,760 --> 00:36:47,520
Hello. I'm Rakkhun.

497
00:36:49,960 --> 00:36:50,840
I love you too.

498
00:36:53,720 --> 00:36:54,800
Vann.

499
00:36:55,440 --> 00:36:56,800
The client's name is Rakkhun.

500
00:36:59,200 --> 00:37:00,440
Sorry.

501
00:37:00,520 --> 00:37:02,280
I thought it was
love at first sight, like…

502
00:37:02,360 --> 00:37:03,880
meeting someone
and blurting out "I love you."

503
00:37:05,720 --> 00:37:06,800
You look familiar.

504
00:37:07,320 --> 00:37:08,760
Have we met before?

505
00:37:16,120 --> 00:37:17,200
I don't want to take this guy's job.

506
00:37:17,800 --> 00:37:20,920
The first time I met him,
I had bad luck all day.

507
00:37:22,240 --> 00:37:24,120
It's nothing. It's an easy job.

508
00:37:24,200 --> 00:37:26,000
The client just wants you to

509
00:37:26,080 --> 00:37:29,280
negotiate with the ghost
that's following him.

510
00:37:29,880 --> 00:37:31,280
I don't believe in that stuff.
You know that.

511
00:37:32,720 --> 00:37:34,880
Sorry, I'm not taking this job.

512
00:37:34,960 --> 00:37:36,000
Calm down, Vann.

513
00:37:36,800 --> 00:37:39,880
For this job,
the client says money is no object.

514
00:37:42,600 --> 00:37:44,440
If you pull it off,

515
00:37:46,000 --> 00:37:48,600
it might pay for your studies
in Japan until you graduate.

516
00:37:53,800 --> 00:37:55,360
I'm willing to pay whatever it takes.

517
00:37:57,120 --> 00:37:59,120
Just get rid of the ghost
that's following me.

518
00:37:59,720 --> 00:38:01,040
I don't want to be single my whole life.

519
00:38:01,120 --> 00:38:03,240
Come on, be serious.

520
00:38:03,320 --> 00:38:05,320
This isn't funny.
What does this have to do with dating?

521
00:38:06,880 --> 00:38:08,280
I've never seen the ghost clearly,

522
00:38:08,880 --> 00:38:10,760
but every person I date gets haunted

523
00:38:11,440 --> 00:38:13,200
until they all disappear from my life.

524
00:38:14,120 --> 00:38:16,200
Please talk to that ghost for me.

525
00:38:16,280 --> 00:38:18,200
Tell it to get out of my life.

526
00:38:18,280 --> 00:38:21,000
But I don't know how or
what to say to drive out a ghost.

527
00:38:21,080 --> 00:38:22,120
Pick someone else.

528
00:38:22,720 --> 00:38:24,160
But the budget for this job
is one million.

529
00:38:30,480 --> 00:38:32,720
Just get rid of the ghost
that's following me,

530
00:38:32,800 --> 00:38:34,360
and the money is yours.

531
00:38:42,320 --> 00:38:43,640
THE CROW CLUB - EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT

532
00:38:50,560 --> 00:38:51,400
I don't like crowds.

533
00:38:52,000 --> 00:38:53,320
At the audition, there'll only be
the label manager

534
00:38:53,400 --> 00:38:54,360
and two board members.

535
00:38:59,040 --> 00:39:00,320
I don't want to be an idol.

536
00:39:00,400 --> 00:39:02,200
When you joined this club,

537
00:39:02,720 --> 00:39:04,440
you said you wouldn't pick
and choose jobs.

538
00:39:08,480 --> 00:39:12,640
Don't you dream
of becoming a singer or musician?

539
00:39:13,760 --> 00:39:16,960
I think going to an audition like this

540
00:39:18,040 --> 00:39:20,640
might bring something new into your life.

541
00:39:41,040 --> 00:39:42,000
Wait!

542
00:39:42,760 --> 00:39:43,600
Hey!

543
00:39:44,240 --> 00:39:45,880
Wait! Hear me out!

544
00:39:47,320 --> 00:39:51,240
I'm asking you
to audition with me just once.

545
00:39:51,840 --> 00:39:53,520
And if our band gets to debut,

546
00:39:53,600 --> 00:39:55,560
then we can talk about the contract later.

547
00:39:57,760 --> 00:39:59,200
I don't like talking to people.

548
00:40:00,360 --> 00:40:03,840
But when you sing,
I don't hear anything else.

549
00:40:04,360 --> 00:40:06,320
I only hear your music and your feelings.

550
00:40:11,000 --> 00:40:12,040
Why?

551
00:40:14,200 --> 00:40:15,200
I don't know.

552
00:40:15,920 --> 00:40:17,680
I've never felt this way before.

553
00:40:18,840 --> 00:40:21,480
Your voice really speaks to my heart.

554
00:40:26,880 --> 00:40:28,400
<i>Aren't you going to greet the client?</i>

555
00:40:28,480 --> 00:40:30,360
This guy is the client?

556
00:40:31,360 --> 00:40:32,800
I don't take clients like him.

557
00:40:33,320 --> 00:40:38,120
Tangmo, talk nicely to your employer.

558
00:40:38,720 --> 00:40:41,880
Sis, you can send me to do construction

559
00:40:41,960 --> 00:40:43,960
or fight the mafia.

560
00:40:45,680 --> 00:40:47,840
But I won't take his job.

561
00:40:48,800 --> 00:40:49,760
Tangmo.

562
00:40:50,560 --> 00:40:54,200
But for this,
you're the only one who can help me.

563
00:40:58,200 --> 00:40:59,640
Why me?

564
00:41:16,800 --> 00:41:18,520
What the fuck do you want from me?

565
00:41:19,560 --> 00:41:23,040
You're the one I believe
can help us win this competition.

566
00:41:24,160 --> 00:41:25,440
I've got the brains.

567
00:41:25,520 --> 00:41:26,600
You've got the strength.

568
00:41:26,680 --> 00:41:28,480
And most importantly, Tangmo,

569
00:41:29,920 --> 00:41:31,360
I want this money.

570
00:41:32,640 --> 00:41:33,680
Money again?

571
00:41:34,720 --> 00:41:36,720
You ran away from your father
to live alone.

572
00:41:36,800 --> 00:41:38,880
You're struggling with money too,
aren't you?

573
00:41:39,640 --> 00:41:41,440
We're talking ten million here.

574
00:41:42,960 --> 00:41:46,000
If we win, I'll give you half.

575
00:41:47,040 --> 00:41:48,840
And I'm ready to sign a contract today.

576
00:41:54,800 --> 00:41:57,760
I'm not desperate enough to team up
and play a game with you again.

577
00:41:59,240 --> 00:42:01,160
You don't want to team up with me…

578
00:42:03,560 --> 00:42:05,280
or is it actually

579
00:42:06,840 --> 00:42:07,840
that you're angry

580
00:42:09,360 --> 00:42:10,680
because you still love me?

581
00:42:10,760 --> 00:42:12,240
You've got some nerve saying that.

582
00:42:12,760 --> 00:42:15,040
If you don't feel anything for me anymore,

583
00:42:15,920 --> 00:42:18,640
just treat this
like any other client's job.

584
00:42:19,680 --> 00:42:20,960
Be professional.

585
00:42:22,640 --> 00:42:24,360
Or do you still refuse to take it…

586
00:42:26,400 --> 00:42:27,960
because deep down,

587
00:42:29,560 --> 00:42:31,800
you still can't move on from me?

588
00:42:37,760 --> 00:42:41,920
THE CROW CLUB - EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT

589
00:42:42,000 --> 00:42:46,160
You want a realistic partner
more perfect than AI,

590
00:42:46,240 --> 00:42:49,880
with the ability to make the client
fall in love for life.

591
00:42:51,080 --> 00:42:54,320
But next to it, it says
it's only until the novel is finished.

592
00:42:56,240 --> 00:43:00,440
But you specified
that you only want Talay.

593
00:43:00,520 --> 00:43:01,760
Yes.

594
00:43:02,920 --> 00:43:07,160
I've decided to use him as the model
for my novel's male lead.

595
00:43:07,760 --> 00:43:09,240
No one else is a good option.

596
00:43:12,960 --> 00:43:14,800
Talay has top-tier experience,

597
00:43:14,880 --> 00:43:16,200
and he's worked here the longest.

598
00:43:16,280 --> 00:43:18,000
Plus, he gets five stars on every case.

599
00:43:18,600 --> 00:43:20,640
He performs impressively at every level.

600
00:43:22,280 --> 00:43:23,520
I understand.

601
00:43:24,920 --> 00:43:27,080
But maybe not.

602
00:43:27,760 --> 00:43:28,600
Why?

603
00:43:29,280 --> 00:43:33,280
Because every Crow has the right
to decide whether to take a job or not.

604
00:43:40,880 --> 00:43:42,240
So, will you take my job?

605
00:43:47,240 --> 00:43:50,400
I get that you're so short on inspiration
you had to hire me.

606
00:43:51,160 --> 00:43:52,960
But I'm sure it won't work.

607
00:43:53,040 --> 00:43:55,480
I'm just using you as a starting point.

608
00:43:55,560 --> 00:43:57,720
I haven't even decided
where the story will go.

609
00:43:58,600 --> 00:44:01,200
Maybe the character "Talay"

610
00:44:01,280 --> 00:44:03,160
might go from someone
who doesn't believe in love

611
00:44:03,680 --> 00:44:06,040
to someone completely consumed by it.

612
00:44:14,040 --> 00:44:15,120
Me?

613
00:44:15,200 --> 00:44:16,800
Consumed by love with you?

614
00:44:17,480 --> 00:44:19,400
I've never been serious about anyone.

615
00:44:19,480 --> 00:44:21,400
And I've never come close to
anything called love.

616
00:44:22,560 --> 00:44:25,840
Why would you bet the future
of your romance novel on me?

617
00:44:27,640 --> 00:44:28,840
I haven't thought that far ahead.

618
00:44:29,360 --> 00:44:31,680
But I'm sure it'll go well.

619
00:44:31,760 --> 00:44:35,360
Because my writer's instinct
is never wrong.

620
00:44:37,200 --> 00:44:40,360
Love isn't something
you can set up, Mr. Writer.

621
00:44:41,960 --> 00:44:45,520
Between two people,
there has to be… chemistry.

622
00:44:46,080 --> 00:44:48,000
Something that makes your heart race.

623
00:44:50,000 --> 00:44:51,160
Which I don't have.

624
00:44:53,160 --> 00:44:55,520
You're saying that without even trying.

625
00:44:55,600 --> 00:44:56,720
That doesn't count.

626
00:45:10,040 --> 00:45:12,560
Well? Feel that chemistry yet?

627
00:45:15,000 --> 00:45:16,920
How could you tell from a test like that?

628
00:45:18,520 --> 00:45:19,640
May I?

629
00:45:58,080 --> 00:46:01,400
I thought a famous romance novelist
would be a better kisser.

630
00:46:03,520 --> 00:46:04,360
Is it clear now?

631
00:46:05,120 --> 00:46:06,720
We have no chemistry.

632
00:46:35,960 --> 00:46:38,240
It's time for me to let the clients know

633
00:46:38,320 --> 00:46:40,400
whether you'll take the jobs.

634
00:46:43,960 --> 00:46:46,000
I don't mind whether you take them or not.

635
00:46:46,600 --> 00:46:50,240
But I always tell you
before you take a job

636
00:46:51,040 --> 00:46:53,360
that a job is a job,

637
00:46:54,840 --> 00:46:58,200
and clients are nothing
more than revenue figures.

638
00:46:59,200 --> 00:47:03,040
If any Crow gets involved with a client,

639
00:47:03,920 --> 00:47:05,360
they'll be fired.

640
00:48:07,280 --> 00:48:09,320
<i>Are you sure that if we put on an act,</i>

641
00:48:09,400 --> 00:48:11,040
<i>that ghost will be</i>
<i>dumb enough to fall for it?</i>

642
00:48:11,120 --> 00:48:13,480
Then you have to make it convincing
enough for the ghost to believe it.

643
00:48:15,720 --> 00:48:18,680
You usually look so dead inside
when talking to clients.

644
00:48:18,760 --> 00:48:20,240
<i>What's gotten into you, Vann?</i>

645
00:48:20,320 --> 00:48:22,400
From now on, when you're sad,
look at this bracelet,

646
00:48:22,480 --> 00:48:23,680
<i>and think of me instead.</i>

647
00:48:23,760 --> 00:48:25,040
<i>Don't think about anyone else.</i>

648
00:48:25,120 --> 00:48:27,360
Rakkhun! We're still together, right?

649
00:48:27,440 --> 00:48:29,200
<i>Kan came to talk to me.</i>

650
00:48:29,800 --> 00:48:31,120
<i>What do you think I should do?</i>

651
00:48:32,320 --> 00:48:33,440
<i>Why are you scared?</i>

652
00:48:33,520 --> 00:48:36,240
The ghost should be scared of me.
